From bdb7c25f1939c707f2d3d04695d4543db2aada02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:36:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pilotd: Marathon OS adapters over the shell's D-Bus
 services

When org.marathonos.Shell owns its name on the session bus, the clock,
calendar, contacts, telephony and radio adapters use Marathon's shell
(Alarm1, Settings1 calendar/events, Contacts1, Telephony1/Sms1,
Network1/Modem1/Bluetooth1) instead of timed, mkcal, qtcontacts-sqlite,
oFono and ConnMan. Media (MPRIS), notifications (fdo) and speech are as
on Sailfish; Sailfish's stock-app hand-offs are not available. Without
the shell nothing changes.
